  "hints": [
    "A province is a connected component of the graph whose adjacency matrix you were given. Start by assuming every city is its own province.",
    "Each time you link two cities that are not yet in the same province, two provinces become one. Union-find tells you whether they already share a root.",
    "Scan the upper triangle (j > i) of the matrix, call union(i, j) for every 1, and return the number of roots left (n minus the successful unions)."
  ],
